From: Connor Gow <cmgow08@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: ignore memory notifications for FEX's own arena

Applies to: the FEX submodule, branch ios-port-2607, at 0f8edf8f6383ae8085e0ffac511c789cdae97514
  git -C FEX apply ../patches/fex-arm64ec-arena-notify.patch
app/Madeira/arm64ec-windows/xtajit64.dll is built from this
(build/fex-arm64ec/build.sh).

InvalidationTracker takes IntervalsLock exclusively and then allocates or
frees. When FEX's allocator commits or decommits a span in its own arena at
that moment, Wine reports it back through NotifyMemoryAlloc/Free/Protect on
the same thread and the tracker asks for IntervalsLock again: a permanent
self-deadlock, typically while a DLL is being registered at process start.
The arena never holds guest code, so those notifications are now ignored.

